      "id": "origins-earth-human-history-s028-p00321",
      "source_en": "In these different ways, the huge areas shaded blue on our world maps are just as important in shaping human history as the green, brown and white features indicating plains, forests, deserts and icy mountain ranges on land. Like this dry landscape the geography of the seas has directed our affairs through history. Let's start by looking at the Mediterranean.",
